{"authored" [{"question" "q-114272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x)=({x}^{2}-4x+6){e}^{x}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)$ is concave up on $(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty )$\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(0,\\infty )$\n- $f(x)$ is concave down on $(-\\infty ,0)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7deeb8093b357a3dcbcd5bd7f2e5c13fa17f4e6f03d01cfdf9c0a86ebf42f1d" "basis" 1616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the second derivative of $f(x),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2}-4x+6){e}^{x}+(2x-4){e}^{x} \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2x+2){e}^{x} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =({x}^{2}-2x+2){e}^{x}+(2x-2){e}^{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the function is concave up, we need to solve ${f}^{″}(x)>0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{e}^{x} & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{x}>0$ and ${x}^{2}>0$ for all real values $x\\ne 0,$ the inequality ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ has the solution $(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$ So $f(x)$ is concave up on the interval $(-\\infty ,0)\\cup (0,\\infty ).$\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is concave down when ${f}^{″}(x)<0.$ By similar reasoning to before, this leads to the inequality ${x}^{2}{e}^{x}<0,$ which does not have solutions. So $f(x)$ is concave down nowhere.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7deeb8093b357a3dcbcd5bd7f2e5c13fa17f4e6f03d01cfdf9c0a86ebf42f1d" "basis" 1616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fe74a5f33fb1820ffabf22a6c87527c6ab012dbdae55ed8ef38b4201dc8ed8b" "basis" 1616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7deeb8093b357a3dcbcd5bd7f2e5c13fa17f4e6f03d01cfdf9c0a86ebf42f1d" "basis" 1616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7deeb8093b357a3dcbcd5bd7f2e5c13fa17f4e6f03d01cfdf9c0a86ebf42f1d" "basis" 1616 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "f7deeb8093b357a3dcbcd5bd7f2e5c13fa17f4e6f03d01cfdf9c0a86ebf42f1d" "basis" 1616 "verification" 