" "q-343146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $g(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${g}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={g}^{″}(x)$, we can see that ${g}^{″}(x)>0$ on the intervals $(-\\infty ,-4),$ $(-2,0),$ and $(2,4).$ \n\nTherefore, the function $g(x)$ is concave up on the intervals \n\n$$\n(\\,-\\infty ,-4\\,),\\,(\\,-2,0\\,),\\,(\\,2,4\\,).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/state.json" "file_sha256" "6fca91e185090cdf8e4aaa9a856e0e9f35f737ae1b73e24cbf042deb271228d1"} {"question" "q-343146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c9dad6845bf9eca2532d48ba52f667b28cf0c8fd38509d319edf3111cbe85818"} {"question" "q-343146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/state.json" "file_sha256" "6fca91e185090cdf8e4aaa9a856e0e9f35f737ae1b73e24cbf042deb271228d1"} {"question" "q-343146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/state.json" "file_sha256" "6fca91e185090cdf8e4aaa9a856e0e9f35f737ae1b73e24cbf042deb271228d1"} {"question" "q-343146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14067662/state.json" "file_sha256" "6fca91e185090cdf8e4aaa9a856e0e9f35f737ae1b73e24cbf042deb271228d1"} {"question" "q-343146" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/co